 "title": "IIM Bangalore concludes 2026 summer placements with record 46% consulting offers | IIM Bangalore",
 "text": "IIM Bangalore concludes 2026 summer placements with record 46% consulting offers\n\nWith Healthcare offers up by 70% and surge in Investment Banking and E-comm roles, 30% new recruiters join placement cycle for the PGP & PGPBA cohort\n\n18 October, 2025, Bengaluru: The Summer Placement process for the PGP and PGP-BA 2025-27 cohorts at the Indian Institute of Management Bangalore successfully concluded with all 601 participating students securing offers from 137 organizations during the placement week from October 13-18, 2025. Students received offers across diverse domains, including Consulting, Finance, Product Management, Sales and Marketing, General Management, and Analytics.\n\nMarking a record high, Management Consulting accounted for 46% of all offers, up from 38% last year. Roles in Investment Banking and E-commerce domains, in particular, saw a notable increase, while offers from the Healthcare sector rose by over 70% (23 offers). Nearly 30% of the participating organisations were first-time recruiters.\n\nProf. Nishant Kumar Verma, Chairperson of Career Development Services, IIM Bangalore, stated: “The PGP and PGPBA cohorts delivered an outstanding performance during the Summer Placement Week. The process was managed with remarkable efficiency and professionalism by the Placement Committee in close collaboration with the CDS Office. We deeply value the continued trust of our recruiting partners and look forward to strengthening these relationships further.”\n\nMr. Tapas Ranjan Pati, Head of Career Development Services, stated, “Leading global recruiters shared highly positive feedback on both the students’ performance and the efficiency of the overall process. Management Consulting emerged as the most preferred domain, accounting for 46% of the offers, followed by Investment Banking and Product Management. Legacy recruiters from Conglomerate, FMCG and General Management continue to hire in big numbers.  We would also like to highlight the record number of offers made by Accenture Strategy this year.”\n\nThe Eleven-member student Placement Committee said, “With 601 students, the largest batch among all IIMs, this placement season witnessed strong participation from both legacy as well as new recruiters, with about 30% being first-time recruiters. This season stands as a testament to our institute’s strong industry standing and the deep trust recruiters place in our students.”\n\nConsulting (23 firms - 282 offers): Accenture Strategy (132), Boston Consulting Group (24), Bain & Company (18), Tata Consultancy Services (15), McKinsey & Company (13), Kearney (12), EY Parthenon India (11), Alvarez & Marsal (10), Deloitte (7), PwC (6), Strategy& India (6), EY Parthenon Singapore (4), L.E.K Consulting (3), NRI Consulting (3), Oliver Wyman (3), YCP Auctus (3), Capgemini (2), Guitcom Consulting (2), Simon-Kucher & Partners (2), Strategy& Middle East (2), TransformationX (2), Black Brix (1), EY - GDS (1).\n\nFinance/Banking/Investments (35 firms – 86 offers): Goldman Sachs (10), HSBC Bank (7), Cholamandalam Finance (5), Citibank (5), Navi (5), Avendus Capital (4), IndigoEdge (4), PwC - Corporate Finance and Investment Banking (4), EY India Investment Banking (3), ICICI Bank (3), IIFL Capital (3), SMBC Bank (3), Axis Capital (2), Bank of America (2), BugleRock Capital (2), Deutsche Bank (2), Edelweiss Alternatives (2), JP Morgan Chase & Co. (2), UTI AMC (2), Abhinandhan Ventures (1), Arpwood Capital (1), Axis Bank (1), Barclays (1), Blackstone (1), Cranmore Partners (1), Equirus Capital (1), Gaja Capital (1), Jefferies (1), Macquarie Group (1), Morgan Stanley (1), Motilal Oswal (1), Multiples Equity (1), Piramal Alternatives (1), UTI Alternatives (1), WhiteOak Capital (1).\n\nEcommerce/Payments/Telecom/Entertainment (15 firms - 55 offers):  American Express (14), Amazon (11), Pine Labs (5), Cocoblu (4), Jiostar (4), Flipkart (3), Myntra (3), Airtel (2), National Payments Corporation of India (2), Princeton Digital Group (2), BT Group (1), Primes & Zooms (1), Tata Play (1), Tesco (1), Visa (1).\n\nIT/Analytics/Product Management (22 firms - 52 offers): Sprinklr (6), Adobe (4), Booking Holdings (4), UKG (4), World Wide Technology (4), Acko Insurance (3), Data Center and Analytics Lab (3), Eightfold.ai (3), Samsung SRI-B (3), eBay (2), Google (2), Hexaware (2), Nutanix (2), Qualcomm (2), Accordion (1), Apple (1), Intellimation AI (1), Media.net (1), Microsoft (1), Newgen Software (1), Salesforce (1), World Infomatix Cyber Security (1).\n\nFMCG/Retail (15 firms – 45 offers):  Hindustan Unilever (10), Amul (6), AB InBev (3), ITC (3), Mondelēz (3), The Coca-Cola Company (3), Wipro Consumer Care (3), Dabur (2), Diageo (2), Marico (2), Nestlé (2), Pidilite (2), Puma (2), Fast Retailing (1), Philip Morris (1).\n\nManufacturing/Construction/Energy/Infrastructure (12 firms - 29 offers): Tata Steel (5), JetExe (4), ArcelorMittal Nippon Steel India (3), Saint-Gobain (3), Asian Paints (2), Castrol India Ltd. (2), KPIT (2), Maithan Ispat (2), Satyam Auto Components (2), SEDEMAC (2), Sahana Group (1), Samsung Electronics (1).\n\nConglomerates (7 firms - 29 offers): Reliance (6), Aditya Birla Group (5), Tata Administrative Services (5), Vedanta (5), Adani (4), Mahindra Group (3), CKA Birla Group (1).\n\nHealthcare/Education (9 firms - 23 offers): Sun Pharma (5), Haleon (4), Athena Education (3), Medtronic (3), ClaimBuddy (2), Dr Reddy's Laboratories (2), Glenmark Pharmaceuticals (2), Optum (1), Zydus Wellness (1).\n\nNews\nConferences\nMedia Room\nCampus Tour",
